{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Sally Gets a Job at a Magazine"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "I Can't Wait to Start"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 16}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le16ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Will, May, Might"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions you in the future. You can also use the modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is \u2018ll.<br/><br/> You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.<br/><br/>The modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> go before the verb.<br/> <br/>They talk about future possibility or a chance that something will happen.<br/> <br/><span class=\"strong\">Might</span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%).<br/> <br/><span class=\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Oh Sally, you may just be one of the best freelance journalists I know! "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I might start my new job on Thursday. I'll be really nervous."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressing Opinions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can express an opinion using one of the expressions below:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Some people say that...</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">(That's) The/the general consensus\u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">As far as I'm concerned,\u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Personally, I think\u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">In my opinion,\u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Sounds like \u2026 </span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'd say that\u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I believe that\u2026</span><br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">What I mean is\u2026</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What I mean is, you might become a managing editor one day, Sally!  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Sounds like you're going to work long hours!"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "masthead "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a printed list in each edition of a magazine, with people's names "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is your name going to be put on the masthead?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about work with a friend."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to put in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to spend time working "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to put in many hours. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to brag"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to talk proudly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm going to brag to everyone about your new job."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a long way to go "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a lot of work to do "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I have a long way to go before I can become an editor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "managing editor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who supervises the day-to-day operations of a publication "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You might become the managing editor of the magazine in the future!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "consensus"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an opinion that everyone in a group agrees with "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's the general consensus."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le16ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Pretend your friend needs some advice. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose 2 different jobs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Your friends wants to know which of the two jobs to choose in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (10-12) between you and your friend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your opinion about the jobs with them. Remember to introduce your opinion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Proofread your dialogue. Practice reading your dialogue aloud with a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I introduce my opinion."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about different jobs with a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le16ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le16ob03re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le16ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: So, Sally, did you hear from Cambridge Life?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I did!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: And?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I believe that you're speaking to Cambridge Life's newest freelancer.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, well. You're now Ms. Sally Davis, the freelance journalist then?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: That'd be correct.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le16ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: When do you start? What will you do?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I might start as early as Thursday.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: That's great. Sounds like you're going to have to put in a lot of hours.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I know. I'm going to be super nervous.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Yeah but personally, I think it's pretty exciting. Now, I can say I know someone who works for a magazine. I'll brag about you to everyone I know.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Peter, it's just a freelance position. Nothing worth bragging about.", "id": 2, "time": "19000", "image": "engenn5le16ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You might become a managing editor one day!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It will be a long way to go before I get to a position like that.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Wait, so, does this mean your name is going to be on the masthead?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Well, Peter. That is the general consensus when you work for a magazine.", "id": 3, "time": "48500", "image": "engenn5le16ob03re2img02.jpg"}]}}]}, {"id": 4, "type": "text", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: So, Sally, did you hear from Cambridge Life?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I did!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: And?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I believe that you're speaking to Cambridge Life's newest freelancer.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Well, well. You're now Ms. Sally Davis, the freelance journalist then?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: That'd be correct.<br><br>\n\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: When do you start? What will you do?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I might start as early as Thursday.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: That's great. Sounds like you're going to have to put in a lot of hours.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I know. I'm going to be super nervous.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Yeah but personally, I think it's pretty exciting. Now, I can say I know someone who works for a magazine. I'll brag about you to everyone I know.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Peter, it's just a freelance position. Nothing worth bragging about.<br><br>\n\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: You might become a managing editor one day!<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It will be a long way to go before I get to a position like that.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter</span>: Wait, so, does this mean your name is going to be on the masthead?<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Well, Peter. That is the general consensus when you work for a magazine."}]}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about jobs and work. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can say what I'm doing in the future. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can introduce an opinion. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you work? "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " I